{
    "__comment__": "Hardware-free setup for the Expert scan panel (scan.scanWidgetType \"Expert\"): scan programs edited as loops, drives, a step timeline, waits and detector bindings, with presets (MS-RESOLFT, a pulse sequence, a stepped raster) and a report of what the scan engine makes of them. Everything runs on a SIMULATED NIDAQ (nidaq.simulation = true). X/Y are galvo-like axes and Z a piezo-like stepped axis, as in galvo_apd_simple_mock_scan_setup.json; two APDs image the same synthetic sample (mockSample) from the scan waveforms, and a mock camera on Dev1/port0/line7 takes a frame per trigger, so an MS-RESOLFT program on Z can be recorded and reconstructed with SNOUTY. The Expert panel builds no waveforms with signal designers, so scan.scanDesigner and scan.TTLCycleDesigner are null. To run pulse programs on a Teensy, add a teensyPulse section and a scanEngines entry with managerName PulseGeneratorScanEngine: a program on the lasers wired to it runs there (the program's devices choose the engine, docs/devices/scan_engines.rst).",
